{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nClosing a ticket can freeze every other agent's writes to the tickets store for minutes. The\nclose's post-write tail calls `_compact_on_close` (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:92`),\nwhich runs compaction; `compact_txn._compact_locked` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:328`)\ntakes the ONE store write lock at `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:340` and holds it for the\nwhole fold — read, reduce, authorship ledger, snapshot write, retire renames, and the git\nadd/commit. Measured on this host: closing `271c-e88f-3220-4c9b` held\n`.ticket-write.lock.d` from 20:35:52 until its `ticket: COMPACT` commit (72ff0358f7) at\n20:49:45 — 13m53s, one continuous hold. Three other closes the same hour held 2m27s, 2m27s,\n2m41s. Concurrent agents then burn their acquire budget and lose writes.\n\nTwo mechanisms make the hold long. (1) The whole fold is inside the lock even though only the\nsnapshot write, the retire renames and the commit mutate anything. (2) Inside that lock every\ngit call goes through `compact_txn._git` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:41`) ->\n`gitutil.run_git_write` (`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:472`) -> `_with_index_lock_retry`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:339`), which opens with `_store_git_op_lock`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:365`) — a SECOND per-store advisory flock. Its budgets stack\ninside the held store lock: `_STORE_GIT_LOCK_WAIT_S = 30.0`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:209`), `_INDEX_LOCK_ATTEMPTS = 10`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:125`), each attempt up to `_TRANSIENT_HEAD_ATTEMPTS = 3`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:418`) git children bounded by `_LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT = 120`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:468`). Nothing bounds the aggregate: `_compact_locked`'s\n`timeout=30, attempts=2` bounds only ACQUIRING the store lock, never HOLDING it. The 7084\nstand-aside probe (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:121`) cannot help the closing\nprocess, which released the lock ~3s earlier so the store always reads free.\n\nRaw git is not the cost: on this tracker (54,931 tracked files) `git status --porcelain` runs\nin 0.185s and `git write-tree` in 0.014s. The time is nested-lock waiting and retries.\n\n## Approach\nKeep compaction where it is — still on close, same trigger, same result — and shrink the lock\nto the mutation only. Split `_compact_locked` into an unlocked PREPARE phase and a locked\nCOMMIT phase:\n\n- PREPARE (no store lock): `_parse_candidate_events`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:176`), horizon partition, `reduce_ticket`, the strip +\n  `_build_authorship_ledger`, and the status guard. All reads and pure computation.\n- COMMIT (store lock held): re-list the ticket dir and compare against the exact candidate\n  file set PREPARE folded. Any difference means an event landed under us, so the prepared\n  snapshot is stale — abort the pass cleanly (exit 0, no write). Compaction is optional work\n  and a skip is already a documented no-op for correctness\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:92` docstring: the events stay live and the next\n  compaction folds them), so aborting is the honest TOCTOU answer and never a stale write. On\n  a match: take `snapshot_ts` (`hlc.next_tick` writes, so it stays inside the lock), build and\n  atomically write the SNAPSHOT, `_retire_folded_sources`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:238`), drop the cache, `_commit_compaction`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:310`), release.\n\nThen bound the aggregate inside that new critical section. `run_git_write` already accepts a\nper-call `timeout` (`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:476`), but the git-op-lock wait and the\nretry loop are not capped. Add an optional `deadline` (monotonic timestamp) threaded through\n`run_git_write` -> `_with_index_lock_retry` -> `_store_git_op_lock`: the git-op-lock wait\nstops at the earlier of its own 30s and the deadline, the retry loop stops when the deadline\npasses, and each child's watchdog is clamped to the remaining budget. Default `None` keeps\nevery existing caller bit-for-bit unchanged. The compaction commit phase passes a deadline of\n`_LOCKED_GIT_BUDGET_S` (30s) from lock acquisition. On expiry the pass rolls back\n(`_retire_folded_sources` already reverses its renames on failure,\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:264`), releases the store lock, and defers — so a\ncompaction that cannot get its git-op lock quickly stands aside instead of camping on the\nstore lock.\n\nThis fits because it changes only WHERE the lock brackets, not WHEN compaction runs; it reuses\nthe seams that exist (`run_git_write`'s timeout parameter, `_retire_folded_sources`'s\nrollback, the optional-work contract) rather than adding new machinery; and it restores the\ninvariant `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` already assumes — the store lock brackets a store\nmutation, not an unbounded wait on a second lock.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` — split `_compact_locked` into the unlocked prepare and\n  locked commit phases; add the TOCTOU re-check and the locked-phase git budget.\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` — optional `deadline` on `_store_git_op_lock`,\n  `_with_index_lock_retry`, `run_git_write` (default `None` = today's behaviour).\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_lock_hold_barbet.py` — new regression tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: a normal compaction still folds — same SNAPSHOT content, same retired sources,\n  same COMPACT commit as before the split.\n- Lock-hold: a background sampler polls `.ticket-write.lock.d` every 20ms across a compaction\n  whose prepare phase is instrumented; zero samples show the lock present during prepare.\n- TOCTOU: an event appended between prepare and the locked re-check makes the pass abort with\n  no SNAPSHOT written, no source retired, and the events still live; a following compaction\n  folds them.\n- Budget: with the git-op lock held by a peer, the locked phase gives up within its budget,\n  releases the store lock, and leaves the ticket unfolded rather than holding on.\n- Failure path: a git failure in the commit phase still rolls back the retire renames.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Compaction's expensive fold (parse, reduce, authorship ledger) runs with the store write\n      lock NOT held — verified by a test whose 20ms sampler records zero lock-dir observations\n      during the prepare phase.\n- [ ] An event appended between prepare and the locked re-check aborts the pass cleanly:\n      the test asserts no SNAPSHOT file, no `.retired` source, exit 0, and that a subsequent\n      compaction folds the ticket.\n- [ ] The locked phase cannot wait unbounded on the nested git-op lock: with a peer holding\n      `.git/rebar-git-op.lock`, a test asserts the compaction returns and the store lock dir is\n      gone, with the ticket left unfolded.\n- [ ] Compaction still runs on close and produces the same artifacts — an existing-behaviour\n      test asserts the SNAPSHOT, the retired sources and the `ticket: COMPACT <id>` commit are\n      unchanged.\n- [ ] `run_git_write`'s existing callers are unaffected — the new `deadline` parameter defaults\n      to `None` and the full local gate set plus CI's pytest tiers pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786593883961629001,"uuid":"019e8d10-353e-4552-96dd-3196d8e4f3b8"}